I did six new significant things this game, it was fun.

First samurai quest
First time to kill a quest leader
First intentional self conversion
First time to levelport to castle prior to clearing higher
levels
First time to do Gehennom backwards
First time to map all of the Astral Plane

I had two (or would that be four) goals this game, ascend a
samurai, keep the three conducts: wishless, polypileless,
genoless. I would have given up one of the conducts if
necessary to ascend the samurai.

Akaski the Hatamoto    St:13 Dx:16 Co:18 In:11 Wi:9 Ch:6 
Lawful
Dlvl:1  $:0  HP:15(15) Pw:2(2) AC:4  Exp:1 T:1

Akaski was never a happy young man. Owing to his dreadful
looks and his parents poor typing which resulted in an
inappropriate samurai name, his peers constantly made fun of
him and he had no friends. This left plenty of time to study
and train. Akaski became fascinated with the legends of the
Dungeons of Doom and the Amulet of Yendor and determined to
leave his hateful home village and seek his fortune in the
dungeons with his faithful dog, Samwise.

The first few levels of the dungeon were not so difficult
for a strong young samurai. Two gunyoki were found on the
first level so food was never an issue. A wand was found
which helped Samwise go faster. The second level had a used
armor shop, but nothing Akaski wanted. There was a fountain
but Akaski had read of many evil things that happened to
young samurai who played with fountains. Level three
contained two sinks which Akaski likewise avoided at this
time, there would come a time however.

On descending the stairs from Level 3 Akaski found himself
in a strange area, more open than the corridors and rooms of
the other levels, these must be the Gnomish Mines he had
read about. The mines were dark and ominous so Akaski
returned to the main dungeon until he was better prepared.
DLs 4, 5 and 6 all had general stores. Akaski found a few
things worth buying, jumping boots were cool, Samwise nicked
a few items and Akaski discovered the value of all his
possessions as well as those which he did not purchase. This
was very important to Akaski since ?oID were scarce and the
first ID all didn't come until 15,500 turns into the game.

DL7 had a lawful altar but Akaski didn't have the means to
create sacrifices so nothing important happened now.
Discovering the blessed status of items was much better now
that Samwise didn't have to test every one. Somewhere along
about here Akaski got a strange mental acuity from one meal
and felt healthy from another, Akaski was encouraged. On DL8
Akaski met the Oracle so, of course, on DL9 Akaski found the
entrance to Sokoban.

Only the second level of Sokoban was troublesome to Akaski.
First a tribe of Mordor Orcs disturbed his labors and then
an ice vortex engulfed him, seriously threatening his life.
Akaski thanked the RNG for the /oFire found in Sokoban, the
ice vortex didn't like fire in it's belly! The top level of
Sokoban yielded a magical bag that lessened Akaski's load.
About this time Samwise became a large dog. This was about
6500 turns into the game.

Now Akaski determined to return to the Gnomish Mines. He
felt stronger and had discovered a lamp that didn't burn out
so he could see better and feel safer. Immediately upon
entering the mines, Akaski stepped on a teleport trap. He
was very glad he had not lingered when he first discovered
the mines since he was not well prepared then. MLs 5, 8, 9
and 10 were lit, ML7 was minetown and ML11 held the
catacombs. Nothing exciting was found in the minetown shops
but the temple was co-aligned. 

One misadventure of note came when Akaski became confused
about which armor Samwise liked and put on a cursed hat. He
made up for this by putting on some cursed mithril. The RNG
forgave Akaski and sent a mountain nymph and Akaski was
clever enough to drop all his other possessions before
approaching her.

At about 14,000 turns Akaski had completed the mines and
Sokoban but still had no source of reflection or magic
resistance. Fire resistance was the only other resistance
acquired at this time. Akaski now did the boring work of
digging out several vaults in the main dungeon for gold to
donate to the priest. Even so, Akaski's AC was still
pitiful.

Time was spent at the altar on DL7 and Snickersnee was
received. Two weaponing Snickersnee and a katana was neat,
and pretty powerful at this stage of the game. A black
pudding gave shock resistance, very timely as we shall soon
see. Becoming bored with the altar, Akaski resumed
exploration of the dungeon and the next unexplored level was
the biggest room Akaski had ever seen! He quickly used his
handy /oFire to burn Elbereth into the floor in the event a
retreat was necessary. Then zap, a grey elf hit him with a
/oLightning, exploding two mildly useful rings, warning and
PFSC. After a quick retreat to get better organized, Akaski
prevailed.

DL12 contained the entrance to Ludious but Akaski didn't
want to try that without MR or reflection. DL13 illustrated
the need for improved AC when the monsters in a treasure zoo
made Akaski use 2 b!oFH. And to add to the insult, they
killed Samwise. Soon thereafter Akaski acquired a new pet, a
cat he released from box. The cat quickly proved it's worth
by revealing a polymorph trap, becoming first a titanothere
and then a balrog. The /oSpeed was applied to the balrog and
he was renamed Shrodinger. He was a pain to drag around with
no magic whistle, but Akaski wanted him to go visit most of
the storekeepers and ultimately the minetown priest. Akaski
was really a bitter samurai.

DL14 was a bones level that changed everything. A ranger who
died for no good reason, left behind Magicbane, The Eye of
Aethiopica, his +2 [CoD, one cursed amulet and a cursed
sack. Since he was beyond Sokoban and had no BoH the amulet
wasn't too hard to figure out. So now Akaski had reflection
and a source of MR albeit not one of my preferred sources.
If only he could pick up the Eye he would have a better
source of MR along with the Eye's other nice properties.
Akaski had another scare here. After being blasted by the
Eye, Akaski twice stumbled across that location with auto
pickup on! Very nearly YASD!

The next two levels included the entrance to the quest and a
neutral temple. An experiment with an amulet changed Akaski
to a female about now and she was more bitter than ever.
Even those succubi she had stashed in the higher levels of
the dungeon wouldn't like her anymore. And it was all
Amaterasu Omikami's fault. First he made her ugly, then let
her have a funny name and now he's let her become female.

Here was the origin of Akaski's most diabolical plot. She
would complete the quest, trash her alignment and convert to
Raijin. She would have her revenge and have the Eye for her
own. Excalibur would be a little balky but that was
acceptable. Then Ludious would provide the gold to restore
her protection. 

The first step was an alchemy session. Nineteen db!oFH were
mixed and 14 were consumed. A peek into Ludious showed there
were 3 dragons, though no silver or gray. A long battle
followed, mostly with Akaski standing in the outermost room
letting the hordes come to her one at a time. When most of
the monsters were dead, she went into the outer courtyard
and slew the three dragons. The black and the blue left
scales. The black scales were immediately enchanted and
worn.

The quest was carefully done. Many horrible tales had been
told by the daemons of rgrn of the fearsome Ashikaga Takauji
and his legendary Tsurugi of Muramasa which has been
reported to severe a man in a single blow. On arrival on
each new level the area was telepathically search for the
foe. Once found, a /odeath was readied and a /oLight used at
each opening in the maze to discover what darkness hid.
Finally an unobstructed path was discovered with the nemesis
still four or five steps away.

No honorable fair fight for this girl. Ashikaga Takauji was
dispatched with a single bolt from her wand. But then her
heart sank. One of his minions stepped forward and picked up
"a samurai sword". She foolishly switched to a /oSleep and
zapped the new threat. Jumping quickly into danger she
applied her stethoscope to ensure she was safe and then beat
the helpless victim to death.

Now that she had the Bell and the Tsurugi of Muramasa, she
sat down to ponder her weapon strategy. It would be stylish
to wield the Tsurugi of Muramasa but it wouldn't do as much
damage as Excalibur dual wielded with a katana and there
were all those rumors about the difficulty of removing
curses from two handed weapons. The Tsurugi of Muramasa was
stashed.

Some research proved that the white unicorns scattered about
the dungeon were not going to be as large a hit on her
alignment as hoped. And none of them were on the right
dungeon level. Finally she hit on a plan to kill all the
roshi attending Lord Sato. This worked quite well, some were
killed in one turn providing even more alignment reduction.
About halfway through, her stethoscope told her she was
insufficiently lawful. Not knowing whether that was good
enough, she slew the rest, then just for good measure she
took out her /oDeath and, remembering imagined slights, she
killed Lord Sato.

Making her way back to the neutral temple, leaving the
killing to Schrodinger for now, she anticipated with glee
her revenge. On the altar she quaffed a b!oEnlightenment and
got good news and bad.

You are the Hand of Elbereth.
You have transgressed.                //This looked good
Resistances you might expect.
You are level-drain resistant.
You see invisible.
