this
You have extra luck.
Good luck does not time out for you.
You can not safely pray.

A foo was sacrificed and the deed was done, Raijin accepted
the allegiance of Akaski. Now to fix the luck and buy back
protection not to mentioned regaining telepathy and claiming
the Eye.

As long as she was here she might as well use her two wands
of create monster to see if she could help the luck problem.
She exhausted the first wand, not stopping to break it soon
enough. After about ten zaps with the second wand, she
decided to break it. Argh! The priest was too close and got
caught in the magical explosion. The priest blinded Akaski
and the other monsters summoned began attacking as well. I
think she could have escaped, but the RGN stepped in again
and forgave another stupidity by having a quantum mechanic
teleport her out of danger.

The aforementioned tasks were done. The best she could do
for luck was throw some named valuable gems to a gray
unicorn. (ID had been a big problem all game). Akaski
returned to the angry priest with a b?oTaming, to no avail.
There was nothing left but to set Shrodinger on the priest
so Akaski could use the altar in peace. BTW, I never could
get Schrodinger to drop his random long sword for Croesus'
+2 two handed sword. I guess it was because he was wearing a
shield and wasn't smart enough to remove it in order to use
the superior weapon.

By now Akaski had found two magic markers and 2 ?oCharging
and wanted to start making some serious improvements to the
AC but also wanted to see what was in the castle armory in
hopes of some special armor before deciding what to enchant.
Somewhere during the quest a tengu had given teleport
control, so she quickly skipped to the VotD and climbed up
to the castle back door.

There were two gray dragons but no silver. It was handy they
were on the same side, they were each killed 6 times before
one left scales. Akaski later regretted that. She became
comfortable with MR provided by the Eye and really wanted
silver scales so she could wear the Eye. The first sliver
dragon she met was killed about a dozen time and 17 silvers
were killed in all but none left scales, and she never used
the gray scales!

The good news was speed boots and a [HoB were found in the
armory. Akaski chose an elven helm over the [HoB but never
had enough ?oEA to get it over +5, and later, used several
spells that might have benefited from the [HoB. The speed
boots and elven helm were enchanted to +5. The {CoD had been
stashed in favor of a robe and all potential AK armor had
been fireproofed (plenty of c?oDA). So the AC was now a
comfortable (for Gehennom) -20.

After clearing the VotD with no particular difficulty and
setting up a stash in Moloch's temple with over 100,000z,
Akaski again pondered the best course of action. About 10
!oOD had been saved but there was only one ?oMMap. Finally
Akaski brought out a c?oTele and requested displacement to
DL 60 which landed her on the dungeon's penultimate level.
This allowed Akaski to map this level differently, stepping
in every corner, walking to the end of every dead end. The
VS was found, the area lit, a c= dropped and a path dug to
the stairs.

Now as Akaski went up, corners were skipped, dead ends were
not explored. If the upstairs were quickly located a !oOD
was used and ^T took Akaski to interesting items but the
rest of the level was not mapped. If most of the level was
mapped before the upstairs were found, Akaski mapped the
rest of the level, hoping for that elusive =oLev or another
MM. All stairs were lit, paths dug and food dropped.

Rodney's tower was cleared up to the point of digging
through the final wall and then left for later. Akaski made
a lucky guess and used her only ?oMMap on the level that
contained the entrance to Vlad's tower. Vlad was no problem
as usual. Coming upon Orcus from beneath Akaski was hoping
to displace him from the stairs upon her arrival.
Unfortunately, he had the stairs so she gave him a couple of
whacks and took the stairs when he went to heal. When he
returned, Akaski went down, scribbled Elbereth with
Magicbane and beat him to death while he tried to figure out
what to do. He didn't waste any shots from his /oDeath.

Gehennom finished the final buffing and polishing brought
the AC to an acceptable -38. There was still room for 5
points on the BDSM and 2 points on the elven helm but the
MMs were dry! The accumulated gold was donated and Akaski
levelported to the portal to the wizard's tower at turn
61,252.

The /oDig and /oDeath were applied to Rodney's room and then
Rodney from solid ground but the hell hound went down with
Rodney so he never melted the ice. The book was secured and
Akaski levelported to the VS level. There was some confusion
in the sanctum when Rodney put in an appearance but that was
sorted out successfully. Akaski found a +oRC in the sanctum,
handy as she was a fair spell caster by now.

The trip out of Gehennom was expedited by 9 c!oGL for the
non teleport levels, liberal use of ^T augmented by a few
?oTele on the others. The mysterious force wasn't a big
factor. At DL3 the items saved for the planes were
retrieved, 4 ?oGD, a crystal ball, a /oSDD, 2 /oDig, lembas
wafers and K-Rations, surplus holy water and surplus db!oFH.

Then I did something careless. It was late, I was tired and
I just didn't have the patience to sort the crap and get
unburdened. But the RNG liked this ugly female samurai too
much to let me kill her off, thank goodness. I think I
carried 41 !of HW with me, for example. Earth went quickly.
After the obligatory scrum with Rodney, the crystal ball
located the portal and the /oDig opened the shortest path.

On Air, Akaski peered into her crystal ball again, quaffed
one of her b!oLev and made for the portal. She was engulfed
several times and entertained herself by using her /oPoly
from inside the air elementals. Fire was easy, the portal
not more than a dozen steps from where she entered. On water
she lost faith in he !oLev and donned her [BoL and quaffed a
b!oSpeed. A c?oGD to get the general location and a /oSDD
for the last few steps made Water a breeze. Sigh, she forgot
to take off her =oConflict.

Since she landed left, she headed left, meeting Famine and
showing him her little death stick. Wrong altar. Back to the
middle where Death stood guard. Just outside, in the
original landing area I finally decided to get unburdened,
long overdue. 

About this time an NPC attacked and my stethoscope revealed
a AC in the -27 range! I even missed him a couple of times!
Well, this got my attention, so I stayed after him to get a
look at his armor. Well, he had a +7 [HoOA and a +2
BlackDSM! So I put a monster to sleep in the doorway
separating me from Death and swapped out my BDSM! Silly!
Several turns unable to move with the AC up about 15 and no
magic cancellation. Should have at least put on an "oLS for
the change. But the RNG was still watching out for his ugly
little samurai.

On to the middle altar. Had to fight death a couple of times
and he actually drained some max HP once. This was the right
altar! There was another NPC with a very low AC here so
Akaski decided to kill this one before offering the amulet.
This gained a +7 robe to replace the +5 robe she was
wearing.

Akaski now decided to take on one last unnecessary danger.
She wanted to see all of the astral plane, not just the
three temples, the whole thing. There were 2 or 3 /oDeath
left and they probably weren't necessary with the +7
Excalibur and a +7 katana, expert at long sword and two
weapon combat with 18/** strength. Pestilence did make her
ill once. If the second try with the unihorn had failed it
was time to eat the eucalyptus leaf!

So here we go, 2,159 after launching from the VotD to meet
Rodney:

